{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-77799" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$|\\begin{aligned}-7 & -1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -5 & -7\\end{aligned}|=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040832/state.json" "file_sha256" "66957468364924e0d88f073f88579bb8126c0661e2a19cd104e310f958496971"} {"question" "q-77799" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The $2$nd row of the matrix contains two zeros, more than any other row. So, using a Laplace expansion along the $2$nd row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-7 & -1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -5 & -7\\end{aligned}| & =3\\cdot {C}_{21}+(-6)\\cdot {C}_{22}+0\\cdot {C}_{23}+0\\cdot {C}_{24} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & -7\\end{aligned}|+(-6)\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-7 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -5 & -7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & -7\\end{aligned}|-6\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-7 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -5 & -7\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040832/state.json" "file_sha256" "66957468364924e0d88f073f88579bb8126c0661e2a19cd104e310f958496971"} {"question" "q-77799" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040832/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7adbcc7d52bf654d087d6f7659d0f66e0953a7b1d71173c43b6e23d57ef5d320"} {"question" "q-77799" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040832/state.json" "file_sha256" "66957468364924e0d88f073f88579bb8126c0661e2a19cd104e310f958496971"} {"question" "q-77799" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & -7\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & -7\\end{aligned}|-6\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-7 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -5 & -7\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "-6\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & -7\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & -7\\end{aligned}|+6\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-7 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -5 & -7\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "6\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & -7\\end{aligned}|-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-7 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -5 & -7\\end{aligned}|"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040832/state.json" "file_sha256" "66957468364924e0d88f073f88579bb8126c0661e2a19cd104e310f958496971"} {"question" "q-77799" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & -7\\end{aligned}|-6\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-7 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -5 & -7\\end{aligned}|"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040832/state.json" "file_sha256" "66957468364924e0d88f073f88579bb8126c0661e2a19cd104e310f958496971"} {"question" "q-69950" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -1 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}|=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040832/state.json" "file_sha256" "66957468364924e0d88f073f88579bb8126c0661e2a19cd104e310f958496971"} {"question" "q-69950" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The $3$rd row of the matrix contains three zeros, more than any other row. So using a Laplace expansion along the $3$rd row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -1 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{31}+0\\cdot {C}_{32}+0\\cdot {C}_{33}+2\\cdot {C}_{34} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{3+4}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040832/state.json" "file_sha256" "66957468364924e0d88f073f88579bb8126c0661e2a19cd104e310f958496971"} {"question" "q-69950" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040832/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7adbcc7d52bf654d087d6f7659d0f66e0953a7b1d71173c43b6e23d57ef5d320"} {"question" "q-69950" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040832/state.json" "file_sha256" "66957468364924e0d88f073f88579bb8126c0661e2a19cd104e310f958496971"} {"question" "q-69950" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}|"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040832/state.json" "file_sha256" "66957468364924e0d88f073f88579bb8126c0661e2a19cd104e310f958496971"} {"question" "q-69950" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}|"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040832/state.json" "file_sha256" "66957468364924e0d88f073f88579bb8126c0661e2a19cd104e310f958496971"} {"question" "q-77798" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -4 & -3 & 8 \\\\ 9 & 5 & -3 & -6 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 7 & 0\\end{aligned}|=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040832/state.json" "file_sha256" "66957468364924e0d88f073f88579bb8126c0661e2a19cd104e310f958496971"} {"question" "q-77798" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The $1$rst row of the matrix contains two zeros, more than any other row. So using a Laplace expansion along the $1$st row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -4 & -3 & 8 \\\\ 9 & 5 & -3 & -6 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 7 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{11}+-3\\cdot {C}_{12}+2\\cdot {C}_{13}+0\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & =-3\\cdot (-1)^{1+2}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 8 \\\\ 9 & -3 & -6 \\\\ -2 & 7 & 0\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot (-1)^{1+3}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 9 & 5 & -6 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 8 \\\\ 9 & -3 & -6 \\\\ -2 & 7 & 0\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 9 & 5 & -6 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040832/state.json" "file_sha256" "66957468364924e0d88f073f88579bb8126c0661e2a19cd104e310f958496971"} {"question" "q-77798" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040832/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7adbcc7d52bf654d087d6f7659d0f66e0953a7b1d71173c43b6e23d57ef5d320"} {"question" "q-77798" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040832/state.json" "file_sha256" "66957468364924e0d88f073f88579bb8126c0661e2a19cd104e310f958496971"} {"question" "q-77798" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 9 & 5 & -6 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 8 \\\\ 9 & -3 & -6 \\\\ -2 & 7 & 0\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 9 & 5 & -6 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 8 \\\\ 9 & -3 & -6 \\\\ -2 & 7 & 0\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 8 \\\\ 9 & -3 & -6 \\\\ -2 & 7 & 0\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 9 & 5 & -6 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 8 \\\\ 9 & -3 & -6 \\\\ -2 & 7 & 0\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 9 & 5 & -6 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}|"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040832/state.json" "file_sha256" "669574683